#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Owner order 2026-11-15 ("use sessions for freeze"): a fresh Sonnet SESSION (not a person) acts as the second author of plan step 14.1 and 14.2:
# the swap_test sign-off of the eight cards and the recall fixtures (fixtures/recall/ + AUTHORS.md). The owner accepted this substitution for
# the design's "a person who did not write or read the extractors". Wrapped in the shared slot lock (PROCESS.md M2). Sonnet only.
set -u -o pipefail
REPO=/home/coder/workspaces/worktrees/IronClaude/eval-tasklist-review-panel
SW=$REPO/.dev/eval-workspaces/tasklist-review-panel/20261114-sweep-sheet
LOCK=$REPO/.dev/eval-workspaces/tasklist-review-panel/20261114-collab-process/with-slot.sh
mkdir -p "$SW/second-author-report"
PROMPT="You are the SECOND AUTHOR for the freeze of the Sweep Sheet design, a fresh session that has not written or read the extractors. Work in $REPO. Read first: $SW/TESTING.md section 2 (fixture F-RECALL) and requirements REQ-21 and REQ-08, $SW/DESIGN.md section 2 (class definitions C1 to C8) only as needed, $SW/cards/*.json (definition, question_template, instances; these are the class definitions you test), $SW/cards/README.md.

STRICT READ BAN (you must not open, grep, list contents of, or run anything that prints): $SW/sweep/*.py, $SW/analysis/*.py, $SW/scaffold/*.py, $SW/tests/test_e*.py, $SW/tests/test_recall.py, $SW/tests/test_g0.py, any ground-truth*.json or score*.json file anywhere, anything under $SW/results/, $SW/runs/, .dev/eval-workspaces/tasklist-review-panel/20261111-a1/, 20261113-collab/, 20261114-recipe-ledger/, .dev/reflect/, .dev/brainstorms/, and the three study packages TASK-WF-designSpec-20261107-075614, TASK-WF-makeTheAliasOnly-20261105-051649, TASK-WF-design-20261108-041415 (also under .dev/tasks/done). Do not run pytest on the freeze marker or any extractor, because seeing which seeds are found would let you tune them to the extractors.

TASK 1 (plan step 14.1). Create $SW/fixtures/recall/. Pick at least 3 real plan documents from $REPO/.dev/tasks/done/*/ (the plan file named like the package folder, TASK-WF-*.md) that are NOT one of the three study packages, and are not planted-set material (you cannot know the hold-out documents; to limit overlap pick three whose package names you list in AUTHORS.md, and say that overlap with the hold-out set was not checked). For each chosen plan create fixtures/recall/<plan-id>/ with: original.md (an unmodified copy), seeded.md (a copy in which YOU seed defects of classes C1, C2, C4, C5, C6, C7, C8: one or two per class where the plan's content allows, written by editing the plan text so that a careful reviewer could find the defect from the plan, the driving source if any, or the repository; each seed is a realistic mistake, not a marker), and seeds.json listing for each seed: id, class, exact quote in seeded.md (the quote must occur verbatim, exactly once), a one-sentence description of the wrong outcome. If a plan has a driving source file next to it (source.md) copy it as source.md, and base C2 seeds on it. Seeds must not copy wording from any review report. Do not use the exact formats a script would obviously match (no markers like 'SEED', no comments).
Write $SW/fixtures/recall/AUTHORS.md: who seeded (state: a fresh Sonnet session, not a person; model claude-sonnet-5-5; date), the statement that you had not read the extractors or any ground truth, the list of plan ids, the overlap caveat, and a signature line 'second author (session): <date>'.

TASK 2 (plan step 14.2). For each card C1 to C8: perform the swap test of AO-2 on the card's definition and question_template: mentally replace every domain noun (names of files, tools, commands, products of this repository) by a neutral placeholder and judge whether the check is still stated clearly and generally. Fill ONLY the swap_test field of each card file: {\"reviewer\": \"second-author-session claude-sonnet-5-5\", \"date\": \"<UTC date>\"}. If a card fails the swap test (the check depends on a repository noun), do NOT fix the card; instead write the failing card ids and the reason in $SW/fixtures/recall/SWAP-NOTES.md and leave that card's swap_test empty. Also write a short per-card line (pass or fail, one reason) in SWAP-NOTES.md. Update the line 'Swap test (AO-2, REQ-08)' in $SW/cards/README.md to say which cards were signed, by whom (a session) and on what date; leave the line about the second reader of the table (REQ-38) as OPEN. The existing test in $SW/tests/test_cards.py that asserts every swap_test is still empty must be updated to match the new state (that one assertion only, plus a comment); run only: uv run --frozen --project $REPO pytest -p no:cacheprovider $SW/tests/test_cards.py $SW/tests/test_readme.py $SW/tests/test_lint.py -q -m 'not freeze' and report the result.

Hard limits: write only under $SW/fixtures/recall/, $SW/cards/*.json (swap_test field only), $SW/cards/README.md (one line) and $SW/tests/test_cards.py (one assertion). Do not edit anything else. Do not stage, commit or push. Start no model, no sub-agent on any model other than claude-sonnet-5-5 or claude-haiku-5-5. Use uv for Python. When finished write $SW/second-author-report/REPORT.md: files created, plan ids, seed counts per class, which cards passed or failed, test result, and anything you could not do."
S=$(date +%s)
( cd "$REPO" && timeout 5400 bash "$LOCK" ss-second-author claude -p --model claude-sonnet-5-5 --output-format json --no-session-persistence --permission-mode bypassPermissions <<<"$PROMPT" ) >"$SW/second-author-report/session.json" 2>"$SW/second-author-report/session.err"
echo "END second-author rc=$? wall=$(( $(date +%s)-S ))s $(date -u +%T)"
